### Get Applications

This endpoint makes an HTTP GET request to retrieve a list of applications.

#### Request Body

This request does not require a request body.

#### Response

``` json
{
  "type": "array",
  "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The unique identifier of the application."
      },
      "name": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The name of the application."
      },
      "enabled": {
        "type": "boolean",
        "description": "Indicates whether the application is enabled."
      },
      "type": {
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The type of the application."
      },
      "secretExpiration": {
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The expiration of the application's secret."
      },
      "validationToken": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The validation token for the application."
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

### Retrieve Application Scopes

The endpoint makes an HTTP GET request to retrieve the scopes of applications from the identity service API.

#### Response

The response of this request is an array of objects, where each object has the following properties:

- `id` (string)

- `scopes` (array of strings)


Here is the JSON schema representing the response:

``` json
{
  "type": "array",
  "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "id": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "scopes": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```
